=begin
  panelcontrol.lic

  A GTK3 control panel for the Saga panel scripts (effectsbar_sagapanel,
  exp_sagapanel, timers_sagapanel, messaging, creaturewindow, playerwindow,
  exitwindow, treasurewindow). Two things it does NOT do, on purpose:
  it does not merge those scripts into one process (they keep running
  independently, exactly as before -- this is a separate control surface
  only), and it does not maintain its own copy of each panel's settings.
  Every control here just fires the exact same command that script's own
  *cwXXX/*ebar/*tm/*exp/;send interface already expects (see
  PanelControl.send_command!), the same way as if you'd typed it -- so
  each panel's own UpstreamHook handler stays the single source of truth,
  including its own confirmation echo, validation, and settings save.

  Usage:
    ;panelcontrol                - Open the control panel window.

  Tabs:
    Scripts    - Shows which of the 8 managed scripts are installed
                 (checked against $script_dir), their version (parsed from
                 the file's own header), and whether they're currently
                 running, with Download/Start/Stop buttons. Download shells
                 out to the existing ";repository download <file>" command
                 (repository.lic must be installed and the file must
                 actually be published there -- this panel doesn't hit the
                 network itself).
    <one tab per managed script> - Buttons/dropdowns/spinners for that
                 script's most common toggles, generated from a plain Ruby
                 list (MANAGED_SCRIPTS) rather than hand-built one at a
                 time, plus a free-text "Custom command" box as a catch-all
                 for anything not explicitly wired up (mainly
                 timers_sagapanel's macro/gemstone/bonus commands, which
                 take arbitrary multi-part text). creaturewindow's tab also
                 has an emoji-picker button for the two Empyrean counter
                 icons (see *cwicon in creaturewindow.lic), so those can be
                 changed without typing anything.

  A control here only works while its target script is actually running
  (this panel doesn't start it for you automatically -- use the Scripts
  tab first). Nothing here polls or auto-refreshes; use each tab's own
  Refresh button after installing/starting/stopping a script.

  Author: Claude Code
  Required: Lich >= 5.20.0, gtk3
  Tags: saga, frontend, mod, window, gtk3, control panel, installer
  Version: 1.5.0

  Recently changed:
    v1.5.0 (2026-08-30) - Dropdowns and number spinners no longer change
      value when the mouse wheel scrolls over them (GTK's own default
      behavior otherwise, easy to trigger by accident while scrolling a
      tab) -- intercepts each widget's own scroll-event and stops it.
      :stepper controls (Effects Bar's Column/Row/Icon-text spacing) now
      update their own value label immediately after each +/- click
      instead of only on the next Refresh Settings/tab switch.
    v1.4.0 (2026-08-30) - Effects Bar's Column/Row/Icon-text spacing
      controls are now +/- button pairs with a live current-value readout
      (a new :stepper control type), instead of an "Increase"/"Decrease"
      dropdown -- these only ever have relative *ebar ci/cd/ri/rd/si/sd
      commands, no "set to this exact value" command, so a spinner+Apply
      wouldn't have anything to apply.
    v1.3.0 (2026-08-30) - Controls now read their target script's actual
      saved settings out of the shared lichwindows.yaml and display them,
      instead of every control being a blind fire-and-forget action:
      toggle controls with a known settings field are real checkboxes
      showing ON/OFF as saved, dropdowns preselect the option matching
      what's actually saved, number spinners preload the saved value, and
      cycle buttons/emoji-picker labels show the current value as text.
      Each tab now has its own Refresh Settings button, and re-reads
      everything automatically every time you switch to that tab (same
      mechanism as the running-status notice fix below).
    v1.2.0 (2026-08-30) - Removed the *cwgtk/*pwgtk/*ewgtk/*twgtk "GTK
      window" toggles from every tab (this panel is for driving the Saga
      panel, not switching a script into its GTK window). Fixed each
      script tab's "not currently running" notice going stale the moment
      you started/stopped it from the Scripts tab without ever rebuilding
      that tab -- it now recomputes on every tab switch instead of only
      once at window-open time. Added this window's own Dark/Light and
      A-/A+ font-size buttons to its header bar (same technique as
      creaturewindow.lic's own GTK window: a CSS provider scoped to
      window#panelcontrol), persisted under a new "panelcontrol" key in
      the shared lichwindows.yaml.
    v1.1.0 (2026-08-30) - Replaced commspanel_sagapanel and verbwindow with
      messaging, playerwindow, exitwindow, and treasurewindow, per the
      user's requested managed-script list.
    v1.0.0 (2026-08-30) - Initial release.
=end

no_kill_all

require 'yaml'

begin
  require 'gtk3'
rescue LoadError
  respond ""
  respond " panelcontrol requires the gtk3 gem, which isn't installed."
  respond " Install it with: gem install gtk3"
  respond ""
  exit
end

module PanelControl
  extend self

  # -------------------------------------------------------------------
  # Managed script registry. Each entry:
  #   key:         internal identifier, also the Gtk::Notebook tab key
  #   filename:    exact .lic filename under $script_dir
  #   script_name:  name Script.start/running?/kill expect (no .lic)
  #   display:      tab/label title
  #   summary:      one-line description shown at the top of its tab
  #   settings_key: this script's own top-level key in the shared
  #                 lichwindows.yaml (nil if it doesn't persist any
  #                 settings there, e.g. messaging.lic) -- see
  #                 PanelControl.read_setting
  #   controls:     ordered list of control hashes (see build_control!).
  #                 A control whose current value can be read back from
  #                 lichwindows.yaml carries a :field (the setting's key
  #                 within settings_key's block, or an array for a nested
  #                 path e.g. ["custom_icons", "empyrean"]); one that
  #                 can't (a one-shot action, a free-text list, an
  #                 unpersisted debug flag) simply omits :field and stays
  #                 a plain stateless button. :choice controls that DO
  #                 have a :field also carry a parallel :values array (one
  #                 raw stored value per :options entry) so the combo can
  #                 preselect the entry matching what's actually saved.
  # -------------------------------------------------------------------
  MANAGED_SCRIPTS = [
    {
      key: :effectsbar,
      filename: "effectsbar_sagapanel.lic",
      script_name: "effectsbar_sagapanel",
      display: "Effects Bar",
      summary: "Active buffs/debuffs/vitals panel with countdown bars and resource tracking.",
      settings_key: "effectsbar",
      controls: [
        { type: :toggle, label: "Stance display", command: "*ebar stance", field: "stance_enabled" },
        { type: :toggle, label: "Encumbrance display", command: "*ebar encum", field: "encum_enabled" },
        { type: :toggle, label: "Shadow Essence display (Sorcerer)", command: "*ebar essence", field: "essence_enabled" },
        { type: :toggle, label: "Hard RT/Cast RT display", command: "*ebar rt", field: "rt_enabled" },
        { type: :toggle, label: "Effect names beside icons", command: "*ebar desc", field: "description_enabled" },
        { type: :toggle, label: "Minimal unscaled layout", command: "*ebar min", field: "minimal_mode" },
        { type: :cycle, label: "Toggle horizontal/vertical layout", command: "*ebar dir", field: "layout" },
        { type: :cycle, label: "Cycle Health display", command: "*ebar hp" },
        { type: :cycle, label: "Cycle Mana display", command: "*ebar mana" },
        { type: :cycle, label: "Cycle Stamina display", command: "*ebar stamina" },
        { type: :cycle, label: "Cycle Spirit display", command: "*ebar spirit" },
        { type: :cycle, label: "Cycle all vitals together", command: "*ebar vitals" },
        { type: :choice, label: "Vitals value format", field: "vitals_display", values: ["number", "percent"], options: [["Current numbers", "*ebar number"], ["Percent", "*ebar %"]] },
        { type: :choice, label: "Layout", field: "layout", values: ["vertical", "col2", "horizontal", "row2"], options: [
          ["1 column", "*ebar col1"], ["2 columns", "*ebar col2"],
          ["1 row", "*ebar row1"], ["2 rows", "*ebar row2"]
        ] },
        { type: :choice, label: "Font size", field: "font_size", values: [12, 24, 36, 48], options: [
          ["12pt", "*ebar font12"], ["24pt", "*ebar font24"],
          ["36pt", "*ebar font36"], ["48pt", "*ebar font48"]
        ] },
        { type: :stepper, label: "Column spacing", field: "col_scale", default: 1.0, inc_command: "*ebar ci", dec_command: "*ebar cd" },
        { type: :stepper, label: "Row spacing", field: "row_scale", default: 1.0, inc_command: "*ebar ri", dec_command: "*ebar rd" },
        { type: :stepper, label: "Icon/text spacing", field: "icon_text_gap", default: 0, inc_command: "*ebar si", dec_command: "*ebar sd" },
        { type: :number, label: "Leading icon spacing", min: 0, max: 20, default: 0, field: "icon_space", command_template: "*ebar espace %d" },
        { type: :number, label: "Leading duration/name spacing", min: 0, max: 20, default: 0, field: "text_space", command_template: "*ebar tspace %d" },
        { type: :toggle, label: "Show every known icon (test grid)", command: "*ebar test" }
      ]
